 "nl": [
  "engineering must never reach dev-lab, regardless of any other rule.",
  "No packet from admin may enter engineering, even for services open to everyone.",
  "Any zone may connect to voip over HTTPS (TCP 443).",
  "Allow dev-lab to connect to library using HTTP (TCP 80) and SSH (TCP 22).",
  "Permit any UDP port from engineering to guest-wifi but deny TFTP (UDP 69), SNMP (UDP 161).",
  "research offers DNS over UDP 53 and HTTPS (TCP 443) to every zone.",
  "iot-sensors must accept IMAP (TCP 143) from dev-lab.",
  "guest-wifi must accept syslog (UDP 514) from iot-sensors.",
  "Allow hr to connect to iot-sensors using SNMP (UDP 161) and SMB (TCP 445).",
  "Hosts in hr may reach guest-wifi over SMB (TCP 445).",
  "voip is isolated: it may only reach engineering on HTTPS (TCP 443), and nothing else.",
  "Deny all traffic from research to hr (this overrides any public service).",
  "Block SMB (TCP 445), Telnet (TCP 23) from engineering to library; the rest of any TCP port between them is allowed.",
  "research must accept NTP (UDP 123) from hr.",
  "hr must accept PostgreSQL (TCP 5432) and SSH (TCP 22) and RTSP (TCP 554) from engineering.",
  "dns-servers must accept NTP (UDP 123) and MySQL (TCP 3306) and PostgreSQL (TCP 5432) from admin.",
  "Deny all traffic from voip to dev-lab (this overrides any public service).",
  "dns-servers must accept HTTP (TCP 80) and SMTP (TCP 25) and SNMP (UDP 161) from engineering.",
  "Allow dns-servers to connect to voip using IMAP (TCP 143) and SSH (TCP 22) and SMTP (TCP 25).",
  "voip must never reach engineering, regardless of any other rule.",
  "Block MySQL (TCP 3306), PostgreSQL (TCP 5432) from dns-servers to library; the rest of TCP ports 1024-65535 between them is allowed.",
  "Restrict research so that its only permitted destinations are dev-lab on syslog (UDP 514); drop all other traffic it originates.",
  "Allow research to connect to library using SSH (TCP 22) and MySQL (TCP 3306).",
  "research offers HTTP (TCP 80) and HTTPS (TCP 443) to every zone.",
  "Allow research to connect to library using SMTP (TCP 25) and SMB (TCP 445).",
  "Make DNS over UDP 53 on research reachable from all internal zones.",
  "admin must accept SNMP (UDP 161) from engineering.",
  "Block SNMP (UDP 161), TFTP (UDP 69) from dns-servers to research; the rest of any UDP port between them is allowed.",
  "Allow research to connect to library using HTTP (TCP 80).",
  "Deny all traffic from hr to engineering (this overrides any public service)."
 ],
